// OctopusExampleConfig — ScriptableObject template (contains no credentials)
//
// 1. Use Assets > Create > Octopus Example Config in Unity.
// 2. Fill the config-level ssoTokenSecret (demo HS256 secret for SSO and bridge posts)
//    and the Default Profile apiKey. Configuration presets each need an explicit demo key
//    configured for their advertised auth policy; there is no fallback to Default in that form.
//    Lifecycle Switch community requires a second, distinct community key in
//    forcedLoginProfile.apiKey (Forced Login > Api Key in the Inspector).
//    The global secret defaults to empty when loading an older asset.
// 3. Optional per-profile overrides:
//      apiKey: each Configuration preset key, including someManagedFieldsProfile
//        (nickname managed + forced login); legacy scenes retain their existing fallback
//      authToken: static fallback when the global secret is empty
//      userId, nickname, bio, picture, entitlements: custom demo identity
//    Empty userId uses the complete OctopusSampleFixtures identity:
//      Default: unity-sample-user / John Doe / no entitlements
//      Forced Login: unity-sample-premium / Sample Premium / customer:premium
//      Managed Fields: unity-sample-moderator / Sample Moderator / customer:moderator
//    Connection presets explicitly request none / premium / moderator / both,
//    overriding profile entitlements; legacy scenes use the profile's entitlements.
//    Static authToken is unchanged, so presets cannot change its claims.
//    With neither credential, Connection shows a readable refusal.
//    Bridge posts require the same ssoTokenSecret or a host-provided
//    OctopusScenarioSdk.BridgeShareSigner; static authToken cannot sign them.
// 4. Optional designReferenceUrl supplies the About screen's Design reference link.
//    Empty hides the row.
// 5. Optional apiServerHost overrides the backend OctopusSDK.Initialize and SwitchCommunity
//    target. Host only: no scheme, port or path (api.example.test, not https://…:443). Empty uses the
//    demo backend (api-demo2.8pus.io), where the demo keys, secret and bridge-post setup live;
//    the native SDKs' own default is production, where bridge posts are not configured.
//
// The generated Resources/OctopusExampleConfig.asset is gitignored. Keep its
// credentials local. Production apps obtain tokens from their backend and never
// ship the signing secret. Fixture values are synthetic and contain no credentials.
